    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters August 14th with a balanced offensive outlook, leaning heavily on favorable platoon splits and park factors. **Mickey Moniak** (74.56) is our strongest play of the day; his matchup against Roupp is a goldmine, bolstered by a 14% platoon edge and favorable wind conditions that buoy his ceiling. **Tyler Soderstrom** (70.65) also stands out as an elite start, taking advantage of a high-park-factor environment against Kumar Rocker. While **Seiya Suzuki** (67.64) and **Josh Naylor** (63.09) lack the sky-high surge of **Mickey Moniak**, both offer high-floor production against vulnerable starters, solidifying the heart of our lineup.\n\nThe optimizer faced a difficult crunch in the middle infield, where **Brice Turang** (53.97) and **Travis Bazzana** (54.67) were locked in a statistical dead heat. Ultimately, the decision to slot them both remains a gamble on speed, as **Brice Turang** is being held back by a projected 40% SB suppression rate against the battery he faces today. We are navigating significant headwinds at the top of the order; **Gabriel Moreno** and **Corbin Carroll** are both struggling against the 2.88 xERA of Sale, forcing their scores down to 43.69 and 52.07 respectively. While we are missing the high-upside utility of **Jose Caballero** due to his absence from the official starting lineup, he remains our primary pivot for any late scratches. We are monitoring **Brice Turang**\u2019s lineup confirmation closely, but with **James Wood**, **Trevor Story**, and **Giancarlo Stanton** all sidelined on the IL, our current depth is stretched to its limit to keep our pace in the SB category.",
